Subject: [PATCH] Fix image upload always disabled, wrong cache key, and
 off-brand colors in Chat Buddy
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Two chat entry points exist for the same underlying thread/message
system: /chat-buddy/:threadId (used by Quick Trips, via the already
on-brand ChatWindow component) and /chat-buddy?tripId=X (used by
regular trips, via a separate inline UI in this file). Confirmed both
share the same chatThreads/chatMessages tables and the same
normalizeUserForUI-based privacy protection, so this isn't a data
duplication issue — just two UI implementations, one of which had
drifted both visually and functionally.

Real bugs fixed:
- GET /api/trips/:id/status was registered twice (line ~1930 and a
  duplicate at ~3992). Express matches the first registration, so
  the second was 100% dead code — and it was the one that included
  chatThreadId in its response. The live handler only ever returned
  {status}, so tripStatus?.chatThreadId was always undefined on the
  client. ImageUpload's threadId prop and disabled condition both
  depend on that field, so the image-upload button has been
  permanently disabled for every regular-trip chat. Merged
  chatThreadId into the surviving handler and removed the dead
  duplicate.
- The image-sent cache invalidation used a query key
  (['/api/chat','threads',...]) that doesn't match the key the page
  actually fetches messages with (['/api/chat', selectedUserId,
  tripId]), so even once upload was reachable, sending an image
  wouldn't refresh the thread until the next 3s poll. Fixed to
  invalidate the real key.

Also recolored chat-buddy.tsx and ChatWindow.tsx from raw purple/
blue/green to brand/accent tokens (header icons, canned-message
chips, contact-share button and message bubble, own-message
timestamp color which was still a green leftover against a coral
bubble).

